 131 **Fixed-subsystem bound.** In a family of pairwise block-disjoint STS(N)s, at most w−2 members can contain an STS(w) on the same fixed w-set W. Indeed a fixed pair in W must get a third point in W in every such member; only w−2 choices exist and repeated choices repeat a block. This bound applies even without resolvability.
